# D-WHOLE-PAGE-CAW-PAYLOAD-PANICS-NODE-IN-SCSI-ALLOC-SGTABLES: A/B of the fix
# (caw_manual_bio adds each payload page as its own bvec with __bio_add_page)
# under the test knob that puts the two payload pages side by side in physical
# memory on every whole-page COMPARE AND WRITE (dbg_caw_span_adjacent).
#
# HYPOTHESIS (in the record before the patch): bio_add_page folds a physically
# adjacent second page into the first page's bvec; 6.8's blk_rq_append_bio
# counts that 8 KiB bvec as one segment; __blk_rq_map_sg maps it as two at
# iscsi_tcp's page boundary (dma_boundary PAGE_SIZE - 1); scsi_alloc_sgtables
# then hits BUG_ON(count > nents) at +0x3a1 (6.8.0-101 disassembly: the ud2 at
# 0xffffffff81c47621 is the cmp of the mapped count, R15, with sdb.table.nents;
# the crash registers held R15=2 and RAX=0x2000, the request length).
#
# BUILDS: control ~/src/mxfs-e srcversion 9371C61A4507F1DBC93670B (the main
# tree's sources with the knob, payload pages added with bio_add_page); fix:
# this tree 65863B924040AF5213F2A76 (the same plus __bio_add_page).  The two
# trees' sources differ only in pal/linux/kern.c's payload loop and its
# comments (diff -rq, then diff of kern.c).
# RIG: 2/net/mesh/direct on g2c (test29 test30, 6.8.0-101-generic), where the
# panic was observed; every arm on a cluster freshly prepped from its own tree
# with caw_span=0, so no prep issues a whole-page command on either build.
#
# PREDICTION:
#   control arms (adjc1, adjc2): PANIC in round 1, test29's serial console
#     printing the BUG with RIP scsi_alloc_sgtables+0x3a1;
#   fix arms (adjf1, adjf2): PASS: 3 rounds of umount/mount/100 creates/sync,
#     caw_span_n rising every round, every P-DBG-CAW-SPAN-ADJACENT line naming
#     two adjacent pfns built as vcnt=2, no panic, boot id unchanged.
#
# VERDICT RULES (written before the first lap):
#   CONFIRMED AND FIXED  both control arms PANIC with scsi_alloc_sgtables on the
#                        serial console, and both fix arms PASS.
#   HYPOTHESIS REFUTED   a control arm completes a round without a panic (the
#                        adjacent payload did not crash the merging build).
#   FIX FAILS            a fix arm PANIC, or FAIL on a merged/non-adjacent knob
#                        line or a failed round.
#   ABORT or VACUOUS     measured nothing: read from its own lines and rerun.
#
# Bounds: prep 300 (as tests/queues/p6_span_ab_tcpdirect.queue); an arm 305
# (tests/caw_span_adjacent_ab.sh header, ROUNDS=3).
300 MXFS_EXTRA_MODARGS=caw_span=0 MXFS_FORCE_PREP=1 /home/steve/src/mxfs-e/run.sh 2/net/mesh/direct --group g2c prep_cluster
305 MXFS_NODE_LIST=test29,test30 /home/steve/src/mxfs-e/tests/caw_span_adjacent_ab.sh adjc1 100000 test29
300 MXFS_EXTRA_MODARGS=caw_span=0 MXFS_FORCE_PREP=1 ./run.sh 2/net/mesh/direct --group g2c prep_cluster
305 MXFS_NODE_LIST=test29,test30 tests/caw_span_adjacent_ab.sh adjf1 100000 test29
300 MXFS_EXTRA_MODARGS=caw_span=0 MXFS_FORCE_PREP=1 ./run.sh 2/net/mesh/direct --group g2c prep_cluster
305 MXFS_NODE_LIST=test29,test30 tests/caw_span_adjacent_ab.sh adjf2 100000 test29
300 MXFS_EXTRA_MODARGS=caw_span=0 MXFS_FORCE_PREP=1 /home/steve/src/mxfs-e/run.sh 2/net/mesh/direct --group g2c prep_cluster
305 MXFS_NODE_LIST=test29,test30 /home/steve/src/mxfs-e/tests/caw_span_adjacent_ab.sh adjc2 100000 test29
